 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? Try a right handed pad on left hand with a thin layer of silicone on the side. Many lefties use right hand pads this way. A pocket for your thumb stops it from sliding directly. A thin layer means you can change it mid session if it gets worn. Look for ones with the pad on the side, so you can swap sides. Some even let you swap sides without swap. Keyboards are nearly always one sided. Look for a left hand model if you struggle with the standard arrangement.",
